# Machine manifest for `bin/sync-omarchy`, the Omarchy counterpart to Archfile.
#
# Archfile says which packages to add. This says everything else that makes an
# Omarchy box mine: appearance, the launchers added on top of the defaults, and
# what was taken away from them.
#
# Sections use the same `# --- <name> ---` grammar as the package manifests: a
# marker owns every line up to the next one. Blank lines and # comments are
# dropped. Assumes an Omarchy base install and states only the delta from it.

# --- theme ---
# `omarchy theme list`. A stock theme needs no install; a git theme goes in
# `# --- theme repos ---` below.

Tokyo Night

# --- theme repos ---
# Git themes to install before the theme above is applied, one URL per line.
# `omarchy theme extras` lists what a machine already has.

# --- background ---
# Filename inside the current theme's backgrounds/ directory.

0-winding-road.jpg

# --- font ---
# `omarchy font list`. Must already be installed — the Archfile owns that.

JetBrainsMono Nerd Font

# --- font size ---
# Bar and shell base size, the one value in ~/.config/omarchy/shell.toml.

14

# --- webapps ---
# name | url | icon
#
# Icon is a URL, a path relative to this repo, or an installed icon name. Leave
# it empty and Omarchy fetches the site's own apple-touch-icon, which is what
# these two do — nothing to keep in the repo, and it tracks the real logo.

Linear|https://linear.app|
Superhuman|https://mail.superhuman.com|
Tailscale|https://login.tailscale.com/admin/machines|https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/homarr-labs/dashboard-icons/png/tailscale-light.png

# --- bar plugins ---
# Widgets enabled on top of the bar's default layout, by plugin id --
# `omarchy plugin list` names them. Enabling needs no sudo, so this reproduces
# the bar without running an interactive service installer.

omarchy.tailscale

# --- tuis ---
# name | command | float or tile | icon
#
# No site to fetch an icon from, so this one is committed under icons/.

Zen Octo|zen-octo|float|icons/zen-octo.png

# --- removed packages ---
# Dropped from Omarchy's default set (/usr/share/omarchy/install/*.packages).
# Applied with `omarchy pkg drop`, which ignores anything already absent. Tested
# with `pacman -Qq <name>`, which follows provides -- `nvim` looks dropped in a
# plain diff of the base list, but neovim provides it.

aether
cliamp
fcitx5
fcitx5-qt
foot
libreoffice-fresh
moonlight-qt
obsidian
omawrite
pinta
xournalpp

# --- removed launchers ---
# Shipped .desktop entries deleted from the app launcher. Omarchy reinstates
# every one of these on `omarchy refresh applications`, so they are named here
# rather than assumed gone.

Basecamp
Discord
foot
Google Contacts
Google Maps
Google Messages
Google Photos
HEY
WhatsApp
